e>> <<is a>> <<one-liner function>> <<using generator>> <<expressions to>> <<flatten and>> <<sum numerical>> <<values:>>\n\n```python\ndef sum_numbers(t):\n    return sum(x if isinstance(x, (int, float)) else sum_numbers(x) for x in t if isinstance(x, (int, float, tuple)))\n```\n\n<<This code>> <<maintains the>> <<possession of>> <<recursive logic>> <<but packs>> <<it into>> <<a concise>> <<single return>> <<statement for>> <<those favoring>> <<compact implementations>>. Both solutions provided <<address the>> <<need to>> <<skip non-numeric>> <<data and>> <<gracefully handle>> <<nested tuple>> <<formats in>> <<Python.>>\n\n## Feedback\nSatisfied 1/4 constraints.\n✓ [combination:two_responses] satisfied — Give two different responses. Responses and only responses should be separated by 6 asterisk symbols: ******.\n✗ [detectable_format:bigram_wrapping] FAILED — Wrap every word bigram in double angular brackets, such as <<I am>> <<at home>> <<with my>> <<cute dog>>.\n✗ [length_constraints:nth_paragraph_first_word] FAILED — There should be 6 paragraphs. Paragraphs and only paragraphs are separated with each other by two new lines as if it was '\\n\\n' in python. Paragraph 5 must start with word team.\n✗ [keywords:word_once] FAILED — Include keyword possession in your response.\n\n\n```\n\nYour task is to write a new instruction for the assistant.\n\nRead the inputs carefully and identify the input format and infer detailed task description about the task I wish to solve with the assistant.\n\nRead all the assistant responses and the corresponding feedback. Identify all niche and domain specific factual information about the task and include it in the instruction, as a lot of it may not be available to the assistant in the future. The assistant may have utilized a generalizable strategy to solve the task, if so, include that in the instruction as well.\n\nProvide the new instructions within ``` blocks."}, "raw_lm_outputs": {"system_prompt": "```\nYou are a meticulous ass