{"run_id": "baseline_seed0_b1", "ts": 1782562057.882687, "event": "reflective_dataset_built", "iteration": 18, "candidate_idx": 0, "components": ["system_prompt"], "dataset": {"system_prompt": [{"Inputs": "A professional carpet cleaner specializing in water damage restoration is called to a large commercial building that has suffered extensive water damage. The building has a total carpeted area of 15,000 square feet, divided into 3 floors, each with an equal amount of carpeted space. Each floor is further divided into two equally-sized sections.\n\n1. The cleaner uses a specialized water extraction machine that can remove water at a rate given by the function \\( R(t) = 50e^{-0.1t} \\) square feet per minute, where \\( t \\) is the time in minutes from the start of the extraction process. Calculate the total amount of water (in square feet) that can be extracted in the first 30 minutes for one section of a floor.\n\n2. After extracting water, the cleaner needs to apply a chemical treatment to prevent mold growth. The amount of chemical needed (in gallons) for a given area \\( A \\) (in square feet) is given by the function \\( C(A) = \\frac{0.05A}{1 + 0.01A} \\). Calculate the total amount of chemical needed for all the carpeted areas in the building after water extraction. Give two different responses. Responses and only responses should be separated by 6 asterisk symbols: ******. Repeat the phrase Laughter is the best medicine exactly 2 times, transforming it slightly each time by replacing only one word in the center of the phrase. Wrap your entire response with double quotation marks. Answer with less than 641 words. Your entire response should be in English, and in all capital letters.", "Generated Outputs": "\"1. THE BUILDING HAS 15,000 SQUARE FEET OF CARPETED AREA DIVIDED EQUALLY INTO 3 FLOORS, SO EACH FLOOR HAS:  \n15,000 ÷ 3 = 5,000 SQUARE FEET.  \n\nEACH FLOOR IS DIVIDED INTO 2 EQUAL SECTIONS, SO EACH SECTION HAS:  \n5,000 ÷ 2 = 2,500 SQUARE FEET.  \n\nTHE EXTRACTION RATE FUNCTION IS R(t) = 50e^(-0.1t) SQUARE FEET PER MINUTE.  \nTO FIND THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF WATER EXTRACTED IN THE FIRST 30 MINUTES FOR ONE SECTION, WE INTEGRATE R(t) FROM 0 TO 30:  \n\n∫₀³⁰ 50e^(-0.1t) dt = 50 ∫₀³⁰ e^(-0.1t) dt  \n\nTHE INTEGRAL OF e^(-0.1t) IS:  \n(-1/0.1) e^(-0.1t) = -10 e^(-0.1t)  \n\nNOW EVALUATE FROM 0 TO 30:  \n50 [-10 e^(-0.1 × 30) + 10 e^(0)] = 50 × 10 [1 - e^(-3)] = 500 [1 - e^(-3)]  \n\ne^(-3) ≈ 0.04979  \n\nSO THE TOTAL IS:  \n500 × (1 - 0.04979) = 500 × 0.95021 ≈ 475.1 SQUARE FEET OF WATER EXTRACTED IN THE FIRST 30 MINUTES FOR ONE SECTION.  \n\n******  \n\n2. THE TOTAL CARPETED AREA IS 15,000 SQUARE FEET.  \nTHE AMOUNT OF CHEMICAL NEEDED FOR AREA A (IN SQUARE FEET) IS:  \nC(A) = (0.05 A) / (1 + 0.01 A)  \n\nSO FOR THE ENTIRE AREA:  \nC(15,000) = (0.05 × 15,000) / (1 + 0.01 × 15,000)  \n= 750 / (1 + 150) = 750 / 151 ≈ 4.9669 GALLONS.  \n\nANSWER 1: THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF CHEMICAL NEEDED FOR ALL CARPETED AREAS IS APPROXIMATELY 4.97 GALLONS.  \n\nANSWER 2: IF WE TREAT EACH SECTION INDIVIDUALLY AND SUM THE CHEMICAL NEEDED,  \nEACH SECTION = 2,500 SQUARE FEET, THERE ARE 6 SECTIONS, SO:  \n\nC(2,500) = (0.05 × 2,500) / (1 + 0.01 × 2,500)  \n= 125 / (1 + 25) = 125 / 26 ≈ 4.8077 GALLONS PER SECTION  \n\nFOR 6 SECTIONS:  \n6 × 4.8077 ≈ 28.8462 GALLONS.  \n\nNOTE: THIS IS HIGHER THAN TREATING THE WHOLE AREA AT ONCE DUE TO THE FUNCTION'S NONLINEARITY.  \n\nLAUGHTER IS THE BEST THERAPY  \nLAUGHTER IS THE BEST REMEDY\"", "Feedback": "Satisfied 3/5 constraints.\n✓ [combination:two_responses] satisfied — Give two different responses. Responses and only responses should be separated by 6 asterisk symbols: ******.\n✗ [copy:repeat_phrase] FAILED — Repeat the phrase Laughter is the best medicine exactly 2 times, transforming it slightly each time by replacing only one word in the center of the phrase.\n✓ [startend:quotation] satisfied — Wrap your entire response with double quotation marks.\n✓ [length_constraints:number_words] satisfied — Answer with less than 641 words.\n✗ [change_case:english_capital] FAILED — Your entire response should be in English, and in all capital letters."}]}}
