y)$, and $\\overrightarrow{a} \\parallel \\overrightarrow{b}$. Find the value of $y$. Finish your response with this exact phrase That's all I have to say.. No other words should follow this phrase.\n\n## Generated Outputs\nGiven vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{a} = (2, 3)\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{b} = (4, -1+y)\\), and the condition \\(\\overrightarrow{a} \\parallel \\overrightarrow{b}\\), the vectors are parallel if one is a scalar multiple of the other.\n\nThis means there exists a scalar \\(k\\) such that:\n\\[\n(4, -1+y) = k(2, 3).\n\\]\n\nFrom the first component:\n\\[\n4 = 2k \\implies k = 2.\n\\]\n\nUsing this value in the second component:\n\\[\n-1 + y = 3k = 3 \\times 2 = 6.\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 6 + 1 = 7.\n\\]\n\nThat's all I have to say..\n\n## Feedback\nSatisfied 0/1 constraints.\n✗ [startend:end_checker] FAILED — Finish your response with this exact phrase That's all I have to say.. No other words should follow this phrase.\n\n\n```\n\nYour task is to write a new instruction for the assistant.\n\nRead the inputs carefully and identify the input format and infer detailed task description about the task I wish to solve with the assistant.\n\nRead all the assistant responses and the corresponding feedback. Identify all niche and domain specific factual information about the task and include it in the instruction, as a lot of it may not be available to the assistant in the future. The assistant may have utilized a generalizable strategy to solve the task, if so, include that in the instruction as well.\n\nProvide the new instructions within ``` blocks."}, "raw_lm_outputs": {"system_prompt": "```\nYou are a helpful assistant that solves mathematical vector problems, specifically focusing on determining unknown variables given certain vector relationships. When given vectors (in component form), and told that they are parallel, you should equate their corresponding components using a scalar multiple (i.e., recognize that parallel vectors are scalar multiples of each