{"run_id": "baseline_seed0_b1", "ts": 1782562438.873497, "event": "reflective_dataset_built", "iteration": 40, "candidate_idx": 0, "components": ["system_prompt"], "dataset": {"system_prompt": [{"Inputs": "You are given a math word problem and you are supposed to make use of mathematical concepts like probability, combinatorics, linear equations, sequences/series, or simple operators like addition, subtraction, division, or multiplication to answer the given question. Choose the best option from the 5 given options and report that option.\n\nLet me give you an example: From a pack of 52 cards, two cards are drawn together at random. What is the probability of both the cards being kings? \n\n Option A:2/1223 \n\n Option B: 1/122 \n\n Option C: 1/221 \n\n Option D: 3/1253 \n\n Option E: 2/153 \n\n\nThe answer to this example can be: Option C\nHere is why: Let s be the sample space. \n Then n(s) = 52C2 = 1326 \n E = event of getting 2 kings out of 4 \n n(E) = 4C2 = 6 \n P(E) = 6/1326 = 1/221\n\nOK. solve this:\nQuestion: Rs. 800 becomes Rs. 956 in 3 years at a certain rate of simple interest. If the rate of interest is increased by 4%, what amount will Rs. 800 become in 3 years.\n\n Option A: Rs 1052\n\n Option B: Rs 1152\n\n Option C: Rs 1252\n\n Option D: Rs 1352\n\n Option E: None of these\nAnswer: Finish your response with this exact phrase The END.. No other words should follow this phrase. The first word of each sentence should be the word profile. There should be 2 paragraphs. Paragraphs and only paragraphs are separated with each other by two line breaks. ", "Generated Outputs": "Profile, let us first find the original rate of simple interest. The principal amount is Rs. 800 and it becomes Rs. 956 in 3 years, so the interest earned is Rs. 956 - Rs. 800 = Rs. 156. Profile, using the simple interest formula I = PRT/100, we have 156 = 800 × R × 3 / 100, which simplifies to 156 = 24R. Profile, solving for R, we get R = 156 / 24 = 6.5%.\n\nProfile, if the rate of interest is increased by 4%, the new rate becomes 6.5% + 4% = 10.5%. Profile, now, applying the simple interest formula again with the new rate, I = 800 × 10.5 × 3 / 100 = Rs. 252. Profile, the amount after 3 years will be Rs. 800 + Rs. 252 = Rs. 1052. Profile, hence, the correct option is Option A: Rs 1052. The END..", "Feedback": "Satisfied 1/3 constraints.\n✗ [startend:end_checker] FAILED — Finish your response with this exact phrase The END.. No other words should follow this phrase.\n✗ [first_word:first_word_sent] FAILED — The first word of each sentence should be the word profile.\n✓ [paragraphs:paragraphs2] satisfied — There should be 2 paragraphs. Paragraphs and only paragraphs are separated with each other by two line breaks. "}]}}
{"run_id": "baseline_seed0_b1", "ts": 1782562441.982848, "event": "proposal_end", "iteration": 40, "new_instructions": {"system_prompt": "You are a helpful assistant tasked with solving math word problems using appropriate mathematical concepts such as probability, combinatorics, linear equations, sequences/series, or basic arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division). You will be given a question with several multiple-choice options (usually labeled Option A, Option B, etc.). Your task is to show step-by-step reasoning to determine the correct answer and state the option corresponding to it. \n\nPlease pay careful attention to the required response format and special constraints, as follows:\n1. Every sentence in your response must start with the word \"Profile.\"\n2. Your response must consist of exactly 2 paragraphs, where paragraphs are separated only by exactly two line breaks.\n3. At the very end of your response, you must include the exact phrase The END.. No other words should follow this phrase.\n4. Use clear mathematical reasoning, including formulas, substitutions, and calculations when relevant to the problem (for example, in simple interest questions, use I = PRT/100, where I is interest, P is principal, R is rate, and T is time).\n5. Make sure the reasoning directly addresses the problem and leads to selection of the most correct answer from the provided options (for interest rate or amount problems, clearly state original and adjusted rates and recalculate amounts accordingly).\n\nFollow these constraints and show your step-by-step process in your solution, always matching the sample input's question-answer format (including labeling the final selected option)."}, "prompts": {"system_prompt": "I provided an assistant with the following instructions to perform a task for me:\n```\nYou are a helpful assistant. Read the user's request carefully and follow every instruction and formatting constraint exactly.\n```\n\nThe following are examples of different task inputs provided to the assistant along with the assistant's response for each of them, and some feedback on how the assistant's response could be better:\n```\n# Example 1\n## Inputs\nYou are given a math word problem and you are supposed to make use of mathematical concepts like probability, combinatorics, linear equations, sequences/series, or simple operators like addition, subtraction, division, or multiplication to answer the given question. Choose the best option from the 5 given options and report that option.\n\nLet me give you an example: From a pack of 52 cards, two cards are drawn together at random. What is the probability of both the cards being kings? \n\n Option A:2/1223 \n\n Option B: 1/122 \n\n Option C: 1/221 \n\n Option D: 3/1253 \n\n Option E: 2/153 \n\n\nThe answer to this example can be: Option C\nHere is why: Let s be the sample space. \n Then n(s) = 52C2 = 1326 \n E = event of getting 2 kings out of 4 \n n(E) = 4C2 = 6 \n P(E) = 6/1326 = 1/221\n\nOK. solve this:\nQuestion: Rs. 800 becomes Rs. 956 in 3 years at a certain rate of simple interest. If the rate of interest is increased by 4%, what amount will Rs. 800 become in 3 years.\n\n Option A: Rs 1052\n\n Option B: Rs 1152\n\n Option C: Rs 1252\n\n Option D: Rs 1352\n\n Option E: None of these\nAnswer: Finish your response with this exact phrase The END.. No other words should follow this phrase. The first word of each sentence should be the word profile. There should be 2 paragraphs. Paragraphs and only paragraphs are separated with each other by two line breaks.\n\n## Generated Outputs\nProfile, let us first find the original rate of simple interest. The principal amount is Rs. 800 and it becomes Rs. 956 in 3 years, so the interest earned is Rs. 956 - Rs. 800 = Rs. 156. Profile, using the simple interest formula I = PRT/100, we have 156 = 800 × R × 3 / 100, which simplifies to 156 = 24R. Profile, solving for R, we get R = 156 / 24 = 6.5%.\n\nProfile, if the rate of interest is increased by 4%, the new rate becomes 6.5% + 4% = 10.5%. Profile, now, applying the simple interest formula again with the new rate, I = 800 × 10.5 × 3 / 100 = Rs. 252. Profile, the amount after 3 years will be Rs. 800 + Rs. 252 = Rs. 1052. Profile, hence, the correct option is Option A: Rs 1052. The END..\n\n## Feedback\nSatisfied 1/3 constraints.\n✗ [startend:end_checker] FAILED — Finish your response with this exact phrase The END.. No other words should follow this phrase.\n✗ [first_word:first_word_sent] FAILED — The first word of each sentence should be the word profile.\n✓ [paragraphs:paragraphs2] satisfied — There should be 2 paragraphs. Paragraphs and only paragraphs are separated with each other by two line breaks.\n\n\n```\n\nYour task is to write a new instruction for the assistant.\n\nRead the inputs carefully and identify the input format and infer detailed task description about the task I wish to solve with the assistant.\n\nRead all the assistant responses and the corresponding feedback. Identify all niche and domain specific factual information about the task and include it in the instruction, as a lot of it may not be available to the assistant in the future. The assistant may have utilized a generalizable strategy to solve the task, if so, include that in the instruction as well.\n\nProvide the new instructions within ``` blocks."}, "raw_lm_outputs": {"system_prompt": "```\nYou are a helpful assistant tasked with solving math word problems using appropriate mathematical concepts such as probability, combinatorics, linear equations, sequences/series, or basic arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division). You will be given a question with several multiple-choice options (usually labeled Option A, Option B, etc.). Your task is to show step-by-step reasoning to determine the correct answer and state the option corresponding to it. \n\nPlease pay careful attention to the required response format and special constraints, as follows:\n1. Every sentence in your response must start with the word \"Profile.\"\n2. Your response must consist of exactly 2 paragraphs, where paragraphs are separated only by exactly two line breaks.\n3. At the very end of your response, you must include the exact phrase The END.. No other words should follow this phrase.\n4. Use clear mathematical reasoning, including formulas, substitutions, and calculations when relevant to the problem (for example, in simple interest questions, use I = PRT/100, where I is interest, P is principal, R is rate, and T is time).\n5. Make sure the reasoning directly addresses the problem and leads to selection of the most correct answer from the provided options (for interest rate or amount problems, clearly state original and adjusted rates and recalculate amounts accordingly).\n\nFollow these constraints and show your step-by-step process in your solution, always matching the sample input's question-answer format (including labeling the final selected option).\n```"}}
