 a parabola \\( ax^2 + bx + c \\) is given by  \n\\[ x = -\\frac{b}{2a} \\]  \n\nHere,  \n\\( a = -0.02 \\)  \n\\( b = 0.5 \\)  \n\nSo,  \n\\[ x = -\\frac{0.5}{2 \\times (-0.02)} = -\\frac{0.5}{-0.04} = 12.5 \\] meters  \n\nNow, we substitute this value into the height equation to find maximum height \\( z_{max} \\)  \n\\[ z_{max} = -0.02 \\times (12.5)^2 + 0.5 \\times 12.5 + 1 \\]  \n\\[ z_{max} = -0.02 \\times 156.25 + 6.25 + 1 \\]  \n\\[ z_{max} = -3.125 + 6.25 + 1 = 4.125 \\] meters  \n\nThe puck reaches a maximum height of 4.125 meters at horizontal distance 12.5 meters  \n\n2. The angular velocity as a function of time \\( t \\) is given by  \n\\[ \\omega(t) = 5 e^{-0.1t} \\] radians per second  \n\nThe total angular displacement \\( \\theta \\) from \\( t=0 \\) to \\( t=10 \\) seconds can be found by integrating \\( \\omega(t) \\) over this interval  \n\\[ \\theta = \\int_0^{10} 5 e^{-0.1t} dt \\]  \n\nCalculating the integral  \n\\[ \\theta = 5 \\int_0^{10} e^{-0.1t} dt \\]  \nThe integral of \\( e^{kt} \\) is \\( \\frac{1}{k} e^{kt} \\). Here, \\( k = -0.1 \\)  \n\\[ \\theta = 5 \\left[ \\frac{1}{-0.1} e^{-0.1t} \\right]_0^{10} \\]  \n\\[ \\theta = 5 \\left( -10 e^{-0.1 \\times 10} + 10 e^{0} \\right) \\]  \n\\[ \\theta = 5 \\times 10 \\left(1 - e^{-1}\\right) \\]  \n\\[ \\theta = 50 (1 - e^{-1}) \\]  \n\nNumerically,  \n\\[ e^{-1} \\approx 0.3679 \\]  \nThus,  \n\\[ \\theta \\approx 50 (1 - 0.3679) = 50 \\times 0.6321 = 31.605 \\] radians  \n\nHence, the total angular displacement over 10 seconds is approximately 31.605 radians  \n\nThat's my answer\n\n## Feedback\nSatisfied 0/1 constraints.\n✗ [punctuation:punctuation_dot] FAILED — In your entire response, refrain from the use of . (i.e. dots) as punctuation and in general.\n\n\n```\n\nYour task is to write a new instruction for the assistant.\n\nRead the inputs carefully and identify the input format and infer detailed task description about the task I wish to solve with the assistant.\n\nRead all the as