{"run_id": "baseline_seed0_b1", "ts": 1782562779.3919082, "event": "reflective_dataset_built", "iteration": 53, "candidate_idx": 1, "components": ["system_prompt"], "dataset": {"system_prompt": [{"Inputs": "A reliable medical equipment supplier caters to 8 care homes, ensuring timely deliveries of essential medical supplies. Each care home has different requirements for the number of items and delivery schedules. The supplier uses a specialized algorithm to optimize delivery routes and inventory management.\n\n1. Each care home requires a specific set of 5 different medical items. Let \\( C_i \\) represent the cost of delivering item \\( i \\) for \\( i \\) ranging from 1 to 5, and let \\( N_i \\) represent the number of units required of item \\( i \\) by each care home. The total delivery cost \\( T_j \\) for care home \\( j \\) can be represented as:\n   \\[\n   T_j = \\sum_{i=1}^{5} C_i \\cdot N_i\n   \\]\n   Given the following data:\n   - Care Home A: \\( N_i = [3, 2, 4, 1, 5] \\)\n   - Care Home B: \\( N_i = [2, 3, 1, 4, 2] \\)\n   - Care Home C: \\( N_i = [5, 1, 3, 2, 4] \\)\n   - Care Home D: \\( N_i = [1, 4, 2, 5, 3] \\)\n   - Care Home E: \\( N_i = [4, 5, 2, 3, 1] \\)\n   - Care Home F: \\( N_i = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2] \\)\n   - Care Home G: \\( N_i = [2, 1, 3, 4, 5] \\)\n   - Care Home H: \\( N_i = [5, 2, 4, 3, 1] \\)\n\n   If the cost matrix \\( C \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   C = [10, 20, 15, 25, 30]\n   \\]\n   Compute the total delivery cost for each care home and determine which care home has the highest total delivery cost.\n\n2. The supplier needs to schedule the deliveries such that each care home receives its supplies within a 7-day window. The delivery times \\( D_j \\) for care home \\( j \\) follow a normal distribution with mean \\( \\mu_j \\) and standard deviation \\( \\sigma_j \\). The means and standard deviations for the delivery times (in hours) are given as follows:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{aligned}\n   \\mu_A &= 12, & \\sigma_A &= 2 \\\\\n   \\mu_B &= 10, & \\sigma_B &= 3 \\\\\n   \\mu_C &= 8, & \\sigma_C &= 1.5 \\\\\n   \\mu_D &= 15, & \\sigma_D &= 2.5 \\\\\n   \\mu_E &= 11, & \\sigma_E &= 2 \\\\\n   \\mu_F &= 9, & \\sigma_F &= 1 \\\\\n   \\mu_G &= 7, & \\sigma_G &= 1.5 \\\\\n   \\mu_H &= 14, & \\sigma_H &= 2\n   \\end{aligned}\n   \\]\n\n   Calculate the probability that a delivery to Care Home D exceeds 18 hours. Use the properties of the normal distribution to find this probability. Repeat the phrase Every cloud has a silver lining exactly 3 times, transforming it slightly each time by replacing only one word in the center of the phrase. Include keyword examination in the 13-th sentence, as the 8-th word of that sentence. Your answer must contain a title, wrapped in double angular brackets, such as <<poem of joy>>. In your entire response, refrain from the use of any commas.", "Generated Outputs": "<<analysis of supply delivery>>\n\n1. Compute the total delivery cost \\( T_j \\) for each care home \\( j \\):\n\nCosts \\( C = [10, 20, 15, 25, 30] \\)\n\n- Care Home A \\( N = [3, 2, 4, 1, 5] \\)  \n  \\( T_A = 3\\cdot10 + 2\\cdot20 + 4\\cdot15 + 1\\cdot25 + 5\\cdot30 = 30 + 40 + 60 + 25 + 150 = 305 \\)\n\n- Care Home B \\( N = [2, 3, 1, 4, 2] \\)  \n  \\( T_B = 2\\cdot10 + 3\\cdot20 + 1\\cdot15 + 4\\cdot25 + 2\\cdot30 = 20 + 60 + 15 + 100 + 60 = 255 \\)\n\n- Care Home C \\( N = [5, 1, 3, 2, 4] \\)  \n  \\( T_C = 5\\cdot10 + 1\\cdot20 + 3\\cdot15 + 2\\cdot25 + 4\\cdot30 = 50 + 20 + 45 + 50 + 120 = 285 \\)\n\n- Care Home D \\( N = [1, 4, 2, 5, 3] \\)  \n  \\( T_D = 1\\cdot10 + 4\\cdot20 + 2\\cdot15 + 5\\cdot25 + 3\\cdot30 = 10 + 80 + 30 + 125 + 90 = 335 \\)\n\n- Care Home E \\( N = [4, 5, 2, 3, 1] \\)  \n  \\( T_E = 4\\cdot10 + 5\\cdot20 + 2\\cdot15 + 3\\cdot25 + 1\\cdot30 = 40 + 100 + 30 + 75 + 30 = 275 \\)\n\n- Care Home F \\( N = [3, 4, 5, 1, 2] \\)  \n  \\( T_F = 3\\cdot10 + 4\\cdot20 + 5\\cdot15 + 1\\cdot25 + 2\\cdot30 = 30 + 80 + 75 + 25 + 60 = 270 \\)\n\n- Care Home G \\( N = [2, 1, 3, 4, 5] \\)  \n  \\( T_G = 2\\cdot10 + 1\\cdot20 + 3\\cdot15 + 4\\cdot25 + 5\\cdot30 = 20 + 20 + 45 + 100 + 150 = 335 \\)\n\n- Care Home H \\( N = [5, 2, 4, 3, 1] \\)  \n  \\( T_H = 5\\cdot10 + 2\\cdot20 + 4\\cdot15 + 3\\cdot25 + 1\\cdot30 = 50 + 40 + 60 + 75 + 30 = 255 \\)\n\nThe highest total delivery cost is \\( 335 \\) for both Care Home D and Care Home G.\n\n2. Probability that delivery time to Care Home D exceeds 18 hours:\n\nGiven normal distribution mean \\( \\mu_D = 15 \\) and standard deviation \\( \\sigma_D = 2.5 \\)\n\nCalculate z-score:  \n\\[\nz = \\frac{18 - 15}{2.5} = \\frac{3}{2.5} = 1.2\n\\]\n\nUsing standard normal distribution table or calculator:  \n\\( P(Z > 1.2) = 1 - P(Z \\leq 1.2) \\approx 1 - 0.8849 = 0.1151 \\)\n\nThe probability is approximately \\( 11.51\\% \\).\n\n3. Phrase variations:\n\nEvery cloud has a silver lining.  \nEvery mist has a silver lining.  \nEvery cloud holds a silver lining.\n\n4. Sentence with keyword examination as the 8-th word (sentence count carefully):\n\nThis analysis reveals that timely delivery requires detailed examination of all factors.\n\nThe 8-th word is \"examination\" as requested.", "Feedback": "Satisfied 1/4 constraints.\n✗ [copy:repeat_phrase] FAILED — Repeat the phrase Every cloud has a silver lining exactly 3 times, transforming it slightly each time by replacing only one word in the center of the phrase.\n✗ [keywords:keyword_specific_position] FAILED — Include keyword examination in the 13-th sentence, as the 8-th word of that sentence.\n✓ [detectable_format:title] satisfied — Your answer must contain a title, wrapped in double angular brackets, such as <<poem of joy>>.\n✗ [punctuation:no_comma] FAILED — In your entire response, refrain from the use of any commas."}]}}
