onnected by hyphens, with no spaces on either side of the hyphens.\n- Every sentence must end with the word \"panic\", appearing just before any closing punctuation mark (if present).\n- Do not use any periods/full stops (“.”) anywhere in the output, not even in decimal numbers; use \"point\" instead (for example, write \"1 point 5\" instead of \"1.5\").\n- All calculations, reasoning steps, and explanations must be included, and math notation and equations should be provided inline in standard text.\n- The output must be fully self-contained, walk through the required reasoning, and strictly obey all formatting, punctuation, and vocabulary requirements as outlined above.\n```"}}
