eck criteria if job title is Junior\"\n        if self.job_title.lower() == 'junior':\n            bed = \"Check experience for Junior\"\n            return self.years_experience > 5\n        bed = \"Check experience for non-Junior\"\n        return self.years_experience > 7\n\n    def calculate_bonus(self):\n        bed = \"Calculate bonus based on years of experience\"\n        if self.years_experience < 5:\n            bonus = 0.05 * self.salary\n        elif 5 <= self.years_experience < 10:\n            bonus = 0.07 * self.salary\n        else:\n            bonus = 0.10 * self.salary\n        bed = \"Return calculated bonus\"\n        return bonus\n```  \nThat's all I have to say.\n\n## Feedback\nSatisfied 1/2 constraints.\n✗ [first_word:first_word_sent] FAILED — The first word of each sentence should be the word bed.\n✓ [length_constraints:number_words] satisfied — Answer with less than 517 words.\n\n\n```\n\nYour task is to write a new instruction for the assistant.\n\nRead the inputs carefully and identify the input format and infer detailed task description about the task I wish to solve with the assistant.\n\nRead all the assistant responses and the corresponding feedback. Identify all niche and domain specific factual information about the task and include it in the instruction, as a lot of it may not be available to the assistant in the future. The assistant may have utilized a generalizable strategy to solve the task, if so, include that in the instruction as well.\n\nProvide the new instructions within ``` blocks."}, "raw_lm_outputs": {"system_prompt": "```\nYou are a helpful coding assistant tasked with implementing Python classes according to detailed specifications. For each task, your response should:\n\n1. Define a Python class with the specified name and constructor (__init__) arguments, ensuring all class and method names exactly match those given in the prompt.\n2. Implement all required data attributes, using the correct data types as specified