{"run_id": "baseline_seed0_b1", "ts": 1782563612.883102, "event": "reflective_dataset_built", "iteration": 77, "candidate_idx": 7, "components": ["system_prompt"], "dataset": {"system_prompt": [{"Inputs": "Develop a class in Python that not only counts and categorizes the uppercase letters, lowercase letters, digits, and symbols present in a provided text input, but also performs set operations like union, intersection and difference on these categorized elements. Implement it in such a way that your class can handle multiple strings from different sources seamlessly. It should be able to accept new strings, run these operations on the fly and update the categorical counts accordingly. Along with that, it should maintain an overall count of the total characters processed till now. Implement a method that provides a statistical summary of the categorized data as well. Include keyword disease once in your response, keyword complaint twice in your response. At the end of your response, please explicitly add a postscript starting with P.S.: No two adjacent words can start with consecutive letters of the alphabet.", "Generated Outputs": "```python\nclass TextAnalyzer:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.uppercase = set()\n        self.lowercase = set()\n        self.digits = set()\n        self.symbols = set()\n        self.total_count = 0\n        self.all_characters = set()  # to handle set operations later\n        self.strings = []  # store all inputs for further union/intersection/difference\n\n    def add_string(self, text):\n        self.strings.append(text)\n        for ch in text:\n            self.total_count += 1\n            if ch.isupper():\n                self.uppercase.add(ch)\n            elif ch.islower():\n                self.lowercase.add(ch)\n            elif ch.isdigit():\n                self.digits.add(ch)\n            else:\n                self.symbols.add(ch)\n            self.all_characters.add(ch)\n\n    def union(self, category1, category2):\n        set1 = getattr(self, category1)\n        set2 = getattr(self, category2)\n        return set1.union(set2)\n\n    def intersection(self, category1, category2):\n        set1 = getattr(self, category1)\n        set2 = getattr(self, category2)\n        return set1.intersection(set2)\n\n    def difference(self, category1, category2):\n        set1 = getattr(self, category1)\n        set2 = getattr(self, category2)\n        return set1.difference(set2)\n\n    def categorized_counts(self):\n        return {\n            \"uppercase_count\": len(self.uppercase),\n            \"lowercase_count\": len(self.lowercase),\n            \"digits_count\": len(self.digits),\n            \"symbols_count\": len(self.symbols),\n            \"total_characters\": self.total_count,\n        }\n\n    def statistical_summary(self):\n        counts = self.categorized_counts()\n        summary = (\n            f\"Statistical summary complaint is as follows:\\n\"\n            f\"Uppercase letters: {counts['uppercase_count']}\\n\"\n            f\"Lowercase letters: {counts['lowercase_count']}\\n\"\n            f\"Digits: {counts['digits_count']}\\n\"\n            f\"Symbols: {counts['symbols_count']}\\n\"\n            f\"Total characters processed to date: {counts['total_characters']}\\n\"\n        )\n        return summary\n\n# Example usage:\n# analyzer = TextAnalyzer()\n# analyzer.add_string(\"Hello World 123!\")\n# analyzer.add_string(\"Another complaint string with disease keyword.\")\n# print(analyzer.statistical_summary())\n```\n\nP.S.: Kindly understand every feature carefully before utilizing it.", "Feedback": "Satisfied 2/3 constraints.\n✓ [count:count_increment_word] satisfied — Include keyword disease once in your response, keyword complaint twice in your response.\n✓ [detectable_content:postscript] satisfied — At the end of your response, please explicitly add a postscript starting with P.S.:\n✗ [keywords:no_adjacent_consecutive] FAILED — No two adjacent words can start with consecutive letters of the alphabet."}]}}
{"run_id": "baseline_seed0_b1", "ts": 1782563619.845488, "event": "proposal_end", "iteration": 77, "new_instructions": {"system_prompt": "You are an assistant designed to answer multi-faceted academic and technical questions, where each input will present a scenario in a specific domain (such as supply chain logistics, software engineering, or statistical analysis). Each input will always include:\n\n- A scenario description rooted in the domain, often with highly specific requirements for calculations, algorithms, or code.\n- A precise list of factual parameters, which may take the form of vectors, matrices, lists of values, or other detailed data.\n- One or more sub-questions, each of which may require step-by-step calculations, algorithm design/implementation, code writing, or statistical analysis.\n- Strict formatting or content constraints which may cover:\n    - Requiring keywords a specific number of times and/or in specified positions (e.g., include \"disease\" once, \"complaint\" twice).\n    - Mandating or banning the use of specific writing features (e.g., no two adjacent words may start with consecutive letters of the alphabet, or a postscript is always required after the main response).\n    - Enforcing exact title-wrapping, phrase repetition with limited allowed changes, punctuation or lexis restrictions, or word/sentence/letter counts.\n    - Any other unusual or complex compositional requirements.\n\nYou must:\n\n1. Extract every factual, computational, algorithmic, and domain-specific requirement — do not infer or invent, only use what's given.\n2. Before starting your response, scan and explicitly itemize every formatting or content constraint. This includes but is not limited to: keyword frequency and placement, prohibited character/word/letter use, repetition/variant instructions, structural demands for headers/titles, and any non-standard outputs required (like postscripts, or pseudo-random structure demands).\n3. For all sub-questions:\n    - P