ress his special pages to the dojo floor capturing each step like an artist capturing a muse's dance-panic\n\nParagraph6 The students and Sensei all participated in this odd ritual accepting that Jack’s fascination was part of the dojo's mystique-The notion of heads and bodies living apart without losing their vitality was commonplace here as was Jack’s immortal state which exempted him from aging or harm-He sometimes pondered if his immortality was a gift or a curse but found joy in the subtle dance between bodies and heads around him-panic\n\nParagraph7 Each lesson was a ballet of whisking limbs and bobbing heads-The decapitated bodies moved with blind grace as if guided by a silent music while their heads watched with sparkling eyes from their resting places on cushioned shelves-At times Jack would gently press a head back onto its neck watching the moment of reunion light up the dojo before another playful separation sent the cycle spinning anew-panic\n\nParagraph8 Sensei Cutelle occasionally demonstrated techniques for balance that involved standing on the balls of the feet or using the neck as a pivot point though Jack had no neck base to pivot-rightful-were careful to emphasize respect for each part of the body a sacred temple even in separation-This attitude helped maintain peace in this bizarre paradise where severed parts and whole beings coexisted in joyful symbiosis-panic\n\nParagraph9 The other students shared their heads willingly with Jack understanding that his ministrations were a blend of homage and deep fascination-Their headless selves wandered from corner to corner guided by trust and familiarity while Jack orchestrated a dance between presence and absence-He seldom ventured beyond the dojo walls as Decapita was a world all its own crafted for those who understood that headlessness was but another form of being-panic\n\nParagraph10 As the sun set casting long shadows on the dojo floor Jack's headless body stretched and glanced at the room filled